---

<DocsLayout
  title="Chat Hub & relay"
  description="Configure ilyStream's unified chat, viewer list, auto-relay, manual outbound replies, and relay safeguards."
  slug="chat-relay"
  updated="July 2026"
  readingTime="8 min"
  toc={toc}
>
  <h2 id="overview">Overview</h2>
  <p>
    Chat Hub is where TikTok, Twitch, YouTube, and Kick messages become one feed.
    Relay controls decide which messages should be mirrored across platforms and
    which platforms are allowed to receive manual replies.
  </p>

  <h2 id="feed">Unified feed</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Platform tabs</strong> filter the feed without changing collection.</li>
    <li><strong>Search</strong> filters visible messages by user or text.</li>
    <li><strong>Viewer list</strong> groups currently known viewers by platform.</li>
    <li><strong>Platform emotes</strong> are rendered where ilyStream can resolve them, including TikTok shortcode emoji and supported Twitch/Kick emotes.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="auto-relay">Auto-relay</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Open Live &rarr; Chat Hub.</strong></li>
    <li><strong>Turn on Auto-Relay.</strong> The switch enables mirroring, but messages still follow source and target rules.</li>
    <li><strong>Choose the relay format.</strong> The default <code>[Platform] User: message</code> keeps context clear when a message crosses platforms.</li>
    <li><strong>Select source platforms.</strong> The Mirror From buttons decide which inbound platforms are eligible to be relayed.</li>
    <li><strong>Select targets.</strong> Target Channels decide where mirrored messages may be sent.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    Relayed messages from your own sending account should not be treated like
    normal audience messages in the unified feed. If you see your own mirrored
    messages filling Chat Hub, check that the sender account is configured and
    the platform has a stable username.
  </p>

  <h2 id="manual-outbound">Manual outbound</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Select target channels.</strong> Pick one or more platforms in the Outbound card.</li>
    <li><strong>Type a message.</strong> Keep the message platform-safe; each service has its own limits.</li>
    <li><strong>Click Send Message.</strong> ilyStream sends only to channels with working outbound permission.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    Disabled target buttons usually mean that platform is read-only, disconnected,
    or missing chat send permission. Health Center shows the same information in
    the Relay summary.
  </p>

  <h2 id="filters">Filters and safety</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>No feedback loops</strong>: ilyStream tags relay output so it does not bounce endlessly between platforms.</li>
    <li><strong>Command awareness</strong>: song requests and AI prompts can be treated as commands instead of ordinary TTS/relay content.</li>
    <li><strong>Source account cleanup</strong>: use a dedicated sender account when possible so relay output is easy to identify.</li>
    <li><strong>Per-platform capability</strong>: YouTube and Kick may be read-only until OAuth and API support are complete.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="troubleshooting">Troubleshooting</h2>
  <p><strong>A platform button cannot be clicked.</strong> The channel is probably read-only or disconnected. Open Health Center and check the Relay card.</p>
  <p><strong>Relayed messages appear in Chat Hub as normal chat.</strong> Make sure the sending account is configured correctly and not being merged as a viewer profile.</p>
  <p><strong>Messages send to the wrong place.</strong> Clear targets, select only one platform, and test with a short message before enabling Auto-Relay again.</p>
  <p><strong>Emotes show as text.</strong> Some platform emotes require metadata from the connector. Send a fresh message after reconnecting the platform.</p>

